    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "STANZA. I.—The commentator introduces his comment on this",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Stanza thus इह खलु सकलवसुधेशाशिखामणी राजर्षिप्रवरः श्रीमद्भर्तृहरिर्वैराग्य-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "शतकमेवारभमाणो राजकुलोत्पन्नत्वाद्राज्ञो नीतिशृङ्गाराववश्यमपेक्षितावतः प्रथमं नीति-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "शृङ्गारशतके वैराग्यशतकावतरणरूपे निर्मायेदानीं वैराग्यशतकमेवारभमाणः स्वेष्टदेवं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "सदाशिवं तेजोरूपेण विशेेेषयन्नमति. Râmarshi's gloss, I find, agrees",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "with what we have said on this Stanza in the Nîtis'ataka. He",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "says दिकालौ वेदान्तिनां मते व्यापकौ पदार्थौ तदादिभिः अनवच्छिन्ना न अवच्छिन्ना",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "न क्रोडीकृता अविषयीकृतेत्यर्थः. मान according to the commentator means",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "ज्ञापक, according to Râmarshi प्रमाण. The latter is a closer",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "rendering, though the meaning is the same in both. The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "following Stanza may be usefully compared : स्वस्याविद्याबन्धसंबन्ध-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "मोक्षात्सत्यज्ञानानन्दरूपात्मलब्धौ ॥ शास्त्रं युक्तिर्देशिकोक्तिः प्रमाणं चान्तः सिद्धा स्वानुभूतिः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "प्रमाणम् ॥ This is in the Vivekachûḍâmaṇi (p. 62 St. 477). On",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "this interpretation, and in view of these words of S'ankara,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "एक might be rendered by “principal” rather than “sole”.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "Râmarshi does not say anything about it—Anushṭub.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. II.—There are three classes of men, those who have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "knowledge and they do not care for other people's learning",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "through envy ; those who have no knowledge, and they cannot",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "appreciate ; and those who have high positions in the world, and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "they do not care for learning being proud of their own greatness.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "So that there is altogether but a bad look-out for learning and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "learned men. Comp. infra Stanzas 28 and 91. जीर्ण = absorbed,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "wasted by absorption, comp. St. 91.—Anushṭub.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. III.—अनुपश्यामि = see in prospect. Comp. न च श्रेयोऽनुपश्यामि, Gîtâ",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "I., 31. On the last two lines, the commentary is as follows: महद्भिः",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    }
  ],
